doc:
Every annotation of the book at `book`, by position, for showing them;
none where they cannot be read. Read them with [`load_for_update`] to
change them.

Asks the reader to show a place in the book it has open ([`Goto`]);
any reader takes it. Sent by the table of contents, bookmarks,
search, syncs of the reading position.

Asks for what `change` needs: a focus moved within the page draws
the entry it left and the one it came to again, nothing else;
otherwise as [`ListChange::request`].

What a point of a picker is on ([`DatePicker::hit`],
[`TimePicker::hit`]): the `+` or the `−` of a field, or its value;
fields counted from the left.

Scrolls as `gesture` says: a swipe up a page on, down a page back;
a tap in the lower half a page on, in the upper half back. Whether
it moved.

A button with a drawing of its own instead of a word (an arrow, a
sign), drawn empty for the caller to draw on with the ink it returns;
`name` says what it does, for screen readers and remote control.
